    "result_text": "The full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class with 2 tests) passes and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `contactPreference` as a derived, read-only field on the Owner response \u2014 following the exact pattern already used for `locality`, `membershipLevel`, etc.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (documented as `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a small `hasEmail()` helper that answers whether the owner has a non-blank email (single responsibility: the domain object knows what \"has an email\" means).\n\n3. **`MembershipLevelCalculator.java`** \u2014 Reused `owner.hasEmail()` in place of the inline `email != null && !email.isBlank()` check, so the \"email present\" rule lives in one place.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `contactPreference` mapping plus a small `formatContactPreference(owner)` default method (`owner.hasEmail() ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\"`), consistent with the sibling `formatLocality`/`formatMembershipNumber` methods.\n\nThe logic sits where the other derived-field logic sits (the mapper), the email-presence check is shared rather than duplicated, and no class became a catch-all.",
